<p data-start=3D"4303" data-end=3D"4437" class=3D"">Si vous obtenez un mess=
age d=E2=80=99erreur, assurez-vous d=E2=80=99avoir ajout=C3=A9 le chemin d'=
installation du JDK =C3=A0 la variable d'environnement <code data-start=3D"=
4430" data-end=3D"4436">PATH</code>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4439" data-end=3D"4442" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4444" data-end=3D"4528" class=3D"">4. =C3=89tape 2 : Choi=
sir et installer un IDE (Environnement de d=C3=A9veloppement int=C3=A9gr=C3=
=A9)</h2>
<p data-start=3D"4530" data-end=3D"4660" class=3D"">Un IDE est essentiel po=
ur faciliter l=E2=80=99=C3=A9criture, la compilation et le d=C3=A9bogage du=
 code. Voici les IDE les plus utilis=C3=A9s pour Java :</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4662" data-end=3D"4688" class=3D"">4.1. <strong data-star=
t=3D"4671" data-end=3D"4688">IntelliJ IDEA</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4689" data-end=3D"4839" class=3D"">IntelliJ IDEA est l'un =
des IDE les plus populaires pour Java, avec une version gratuite (Community=
 Edition) et une version payante (Ultimate Edition).</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4841" data-end=3D"5078">
<li data-start=3D"4841" data-end=3D"5005" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4843" data-end=3D"5005" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
843" data-end=3D"4872">T=C3=A9l=C3=A9charger IntelliJ IDEA</strong> : Rende=
z-vous sur <a data-start=3D"4891" data-end=3D"4958" rel=3D"noopener" target=
=3D"_new" class=3D"" href=3D"https://www.jetbrains.com/idea/download/">le s=
ite d'IntelliJ IDEA</a> et t=C3=A9l=C3=A9chargez la version gratuite ou pay=
ante.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5006" data-end=3D"5078" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5008" data-end=3D"5078" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
008" data-end=3D"5024">Installation</strong> : Suivez les instructions d'in=
stallation sur le site.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5080" data-end=3D"5100" class=3D"">4.2. <strong data-star=
t=3D"5089" data-end=3D"5100">Eclipse</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5101" data-end=3D"5185" class=3D"">Eclipse est un autre ID=
E tr=C3=A8s populaire pour Java. Il est open-source et extensible.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5187" data-end=3D"5423">
<li data-start=3D"5187" data-end=3D"5358" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5189" data-end=3D"5358" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
189" data-end=3D"5212">T=C3=A9l=C3=A9charger Eclipse</strong> : Allez sur l=
e site <a data-start=3D"5233" data-end=3D"5288" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"=
_new" class=3D"cursor-pointer">Eclipse Downloads</a> et t=C3=A9l=C3=A9charg=
ez la version ad=C3=A9quate pour votre syst=C3=A8me d=E2=80=99exploitation.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5359" data-end=3D"5423" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5361" data-end=3D"5423" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
361" data-end=3D"5377">Installation</strong> : Lancez l'installateur et sui=
vez les =C3=A9tapes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5425" data-end=3D"5446" class=3D"">4.3. <strong data-star=
t=3D"5434" data-end=3D"5446">NetBeans</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5447" data-end=3D"5575" class=3D"">NetBeans est un autre I=
DE open-source, moins populaire qu'IntelliJ IDEA et Eclipse mais tr=C3=A8s =
complet pour le d=C3=A9veloppement Java.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5577" data-end=3D"5732">
<li data-start=3D"5577" data-end=3D"5732" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5579" data-end=3D"5732" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
579" data-end=3D"5603">T=C3=A9l=C3=A9charger NetBeans</strong> : Allez sur =
le site <a data-start=3D"5624" data-end=3D"5664" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D=
"_new" class=3D"" href=3D"https://netbeans.apache.org/">NetBeans</a> pour t=
=C3=A9l=C3=A9charger la version adapt=C3=A9e =C3=A0 votre syst=C3=A8me d'ex=
ploitation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5734" data-end=3D"5773" class=3D"">4.4. <strong data-star=
t=3D"5743" data-end=3D"5773">Configurer l=E2=80=99IDE avec Java</strong></h=
3>
<p data-start=3D"5774" data-end=3D"6038" class=3D"">Une fois l=E2=80=99IDE =
install=C3=A9, vous devrez peut-=C3=AAtre configurer l=E2=80=99environnemen=
t pour qu=E2=80=99il utilise le JDK que vous avez install=C3=A9. La configu=
ration est g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ralement automatique, mais vous pouvez v=C3=A9rifi=
er dans les param=C3=A8tres de l'IDE que le JDK est correctement r=C3=A9f=
=C3=A9renc=C3=A9.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"6040" data-end=3D"6043" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6045" data-end=3D"6086" class=3D"">5. =C3=89tape 3 : Conf=
igurer un projet Java</h2>
<p data-start=3D"6088" data-end=3D"6225" class=3D"">Une fois l'IDE et le JD=
K install=C3=A9s, il est temps de cr=C3=A9er un projet Java. Voici les =C3=
=A9tapes de base pour cr=C3=A9er un projet Java dans un IDE.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6227" data-end=3D"6270" class=3D"">5.1. Cr=C3=A9er un pro=
jet dans IntelliJ IDEA</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"6271" data-end=3D"6468">
<li data-start=3D"6271" data-end=3D"6332" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6274" data-end=3D"6332" class=3D"">Ouvrez IntelliJ IDEA et=
 s=C3=A9lectionnez "Create New Project".</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6333" data-end=3D"6375" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6336" data-end=3D"6375" class=3D"">Choisissez "Java" comme=
 type de projet.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6376" data-end=3D"6422" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6379" data-end=3D"6422" class=3D"">S=C3=A9lectionnez le JD=
K que vous avez install=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6423" data-end=3D"6468" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6426" data-end=3D"6468" class=3D"">Cliquez sur "Finish" po=
ur cr=C3=A9er le projet.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"6470" data-end=3D"6507" class=3D"">5.2. Cr=C3=A9er un pro=
jet dans Eclipse</h3>
<ol data-start=3D"6508" data-end=3D"6671">
<li data-start=3D"6508" data-end=3D"6574" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6511" data-end=3D"6574" class=3D"">Ouvrez Eclipse et s=C3=
=A9lectionnez "File" &gt; "New" &gt; "Java Project".</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6575" data-end=3D"6625" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6578" data-end=3D"6625" class=3D"">Donnez un nom au projet=
 et s=C3=A9lectionnez le JDK.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6626" data-end=3D"6671" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6629" data-end=3D"6671" class=3D"">Cliquez sur "Finish" po=
ur cr=C3=A9er le projet.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"6673" data-end=3D"6708" class=3D"">5.3. Structure d=E2=80=
=99un projet Java</h3>
