    }

    </span><span><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">public</span></span><span> </=
span><span><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">void</span></span><span> </span><sp=
an><span class=3D"hljs-title function_">performService</span></span><span><=
span class=3D"hljs-params">()</span></span><span> {
        repository.executeQuery();
    }
}
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<p data-start=3D"4203" data-end=3D"4303" class=3D"">Ici, Spring se charge d=
e l'injection de <code data-start=3D"4243" data-end=3D"4255">Repository</co=
de> dans <code data-start=3D"4261" data-end=3D"4270">Service</code> via l'a=
nnotation <strong data-start=3D"4288" data-end=3D"4302">@Autowired</strong>=
.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4305" data-end=3D"4308" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4310" data-end=3D"4363" class=3D"">2. Qu'est-ce que l'Inj=
ection de D=C3=A9pendances (DI) ?</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4365" data-end=3D"4412" class=3D"">2.1. Principe de l'Inj=
ection de D=C3=A9pendances</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4414" data-end=3D"4767" class=3D"">L'Injection de D=C3=A9p=
endances (DI) est un type d'Inversion de Contr=C3=B4le dans lequel les d=C3=
=A9pendances d=E2=80=99un objet sont fournies par un conteneur IoC (comme S=
pring) plut=C3=B4t que par l'objet lui-m=C3=AAme. En d=E2=80=99autres terme=
s, au lieu de cr=C3=A9er une instance d'une classe ou de g=C3=A9rer ses d=
=C3=A9pendances directement, un composant (un <strong data-start=3D"4725" d=
ata-end=3D"4733">Bean</strong>) re=C3=A7oit ses d=C3=A9pendances externes.<=
/p>
<p data-start=3D"4769" data-end=3D"4890" class=3D"">L'injection de d=C3=A9p=
endances permet de r=C3=A9duire le couplage entre les composants et de faci=
liter la gestion des d=C3=A9pendances.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4892" data-end=3D"4933" class=3D"">2.2. Types d'Injection=
 de D=C3=A9pendances</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4935" data-end=3D"4995" class=3D"">Spring supporte plusieu=
rs types d'Injection de D=C3=A9pendances :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4996" data-end=3D"5333">
<li data-start=3D"4996" data-end=3D"5095" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4998" data-end=3D"5095" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
998" data-end=3D"5028">Injection par constructeur</strong> : Les d=C3=A9pen=
dances sont inject=C3=A9es via le constructeur de la classe.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5096" data-end=3D"5202" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5098" data-end=3D"5202" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
098" data-end=3D"5132">Injection par m=C3=A9thode (setter)</strong> : Les d=
=C3=A9pendances sont inject=C3=A9es via des m=C3=A9thodes <code data-start=
=3D"5183" data-end=3D"5191">setter</code> publiques.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5203" data-end=3D"5333" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5205" data-end=3D"5333" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
205" data-end=3D"5228">Injection par champ</strong> : Les d=C3=A9pendances =
sont inject=C3=A9es directement dans les champs de la classe via l'annotati=
on <code data-start=3D"5320" data-end=3D"5332">@Autowired</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"5335" data-end=3D"5358" class=3D"">2.3. DI avec Spring</h=
3>
<p data-start=3D"5360" data-end=3D"5426" class=3D"">Spring facilite l'Injec=
tion de D=C3=A9pendances de plusieurs mani=C3=A8res :</p>
