<h3 data-start=3D"7202" data-end=3D"7274" class=3D"">3.3. Types de configur=
ation Spring : Java-based, XML, et annotations</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7276" data-end=3D"7623">
<li data-start=3D"7276" data-end=3D"7380" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7278" data-end=3D"7380" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
278" data-end=3D"7300">Configuration Java</strong> : Utilisation de la clas=
se <code data-start=3D"7328" data-end=3D"7344">@Configuration</code> et <co=
de data-start=3D"7348" data-end=3D"7355">@Bean</code> pour d=C3=A9clarer le=
s Beans.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7381" data-end=3D"7481" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7383" data-end=3D"7481" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
383" data-end=3D"7396">XML-based</strong> : Utilisation de fichiers XML pou=
r configurer les Beans (moins courant aujourd'hui).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7482" data-end=3D"7623" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7484" data-end=3D"7623" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
484" data-end=3D"7505">Annotations-based</strong> : Utilisation d'annotatio=
ns comme <code data-start=3D"7540" data-end=3D"7552">@Component</code>, <co=
de data-start=3D"7554" data-end=3D"7564">@Service</code>, <code data-start=
=3D"7566" data-end=3D"7579">@Repository</code>, et <code data-start=3D"7584=
" data-end=3D"7596">@Autowired</code> pour configurer les Beans.</p>
</li>
</ul>
