<h2 data-start=3D"3133" data-end=3D"3186" class=3D"">1. Introduction =C3=A0=
 la configuration par annotations</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"3188" data-end=3D"3249" class=3D"">1.1. Pourquoi utiliser=
 la configuration par annotations ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3251" data-end=3D"3403" class=3D"">Avec l=E2=80=99arriv=C3=
=A9e de Spring 3, la configuration par annotations a =C3=A9t=C3=A9 introdui=
te pour simplifier la configuration des applications Spring. Elle permet de=
 :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3404" data-end=3D"3657">
<li data-start=3D"3404" data-end=3D"3447" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3406" data-end=3D"3447" class=3D"">Supprimer le besoin de =
configuration XML.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3448" data-end=3D"3500" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3450" data-end=3D"3500" class=3D"">Rendre la configuration=
 plus intuitive et lisible.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3501" data-end=3D"3591" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3503" data-end=3D"3591" class=3D"">Faciliter la gestion de=
 la configuration =C3=A0 travers des annotations sp=C3=A9cifiques =C3=A0 Sp=
ring.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3592" data-end=3D"3657" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3594" data-end=3D"3657" class=3D"">Am=C3=A9liorer la maint=
enabilit=C3=A9 et la flexibilit=C3=A9 de l=E2=80=99application.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3659" data-end=3D"3708" class=3D"">1.2. Vue d=E2=80=99ens=
emble des annotations courantes</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3710" data-end=3D"3788" class=3D"">Les principales annotat=
ions utilis=C3=A9es pour la configuration dans Spring sont :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3789" data-end=3D"4330">
<li data-start=3D"3789" data-end=3D"3870" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3791" data-end=3D"3870" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
791" data-end=3D"3811"><code data-start=3D"3793" data-end=3D"3809">@Configu=
ration</code></strong> : Indique une classe comme source de configuration S=
pring.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3871" data-end=3D"3939" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3873" data-end=3D"3939" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
873" data-end=3D"3884"><code data-start=3D"3875" data-end=3D"3882">@Bean</c=
ode></strong> : D=C3=A9finit un bean =C3=A0 =C3=AAtre g=C3=A9r=C3=A9 par le=
 conteneur Spring.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3940" data-end=3D"4090" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3942" data-end=3D"4090" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
942" data-end=3D"3962"><code data-start=3D"3944" data-end=3D"3960">@Compone=
ntScan</code></strong> : Permet =C3=A0 Spring de scanner les classes pour y=
 d=C3=A9couvrir des beans annot=C3=A9s comme <code data-start=3D"4045" data=
-end=3D"4057">@Component</code>, <code data-start=3D"4059" data-end=3D"4069=
">@Service</code>, <code data-start=3D"4071" data-end=3D"4084">@Repository<=
/code>, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4091" data-end=3D"4234" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4093" data-end=3D"4234" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
093" data-end=3D"4151"><code data-start=3D"4095" data-end=3D"4107">@Compone=
nt</code>, <code data-start=3D"4109" data-end=3D"4119">@Service</code>, <co=
de data-start=3D"4121" data-end=3D"4134">@Repository</code>, <code data-sta=
rt=3D"4136" data-end=3D"4149">@Controller</code></strong> : Sp=C3=A9cialise=
nt les beans comme des composants Spring dans des couches sp=C3=A9cifiques.=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4235" data-end=3D"4330" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4237" data-end=3D"4330" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
237" data-end=3D"4251"><code data-start=3D"4239" data-end=3D"4249">@Profile=
</code></strong> : Permet d'indiquer qu'un bean est actif uniquement dans u=
n profil sp=C3=A9cifique.</p>
</li>
</ul>
