<h2 data-start=3D"7916" data-end=3D"8001" class=3D"">5. Les autres annotati=
ons : <code data-start=3D"7947" data-end=3D"7959">@Component</code>, <code =
data-start=3D"7961" data-end=3D"7971">@Service</code>, <code data-start=3D"=
7973" data-end=3D"7986">@Repository</code>, <code data-start=3D"7988" data-=
end=3D"8001">@Controller</code></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"8003" data-end=3D"8040" class=3D"">5.1. Qu'est-ce que <co=
de data-start=3D"8026" data-end=3D"8038">@Component</code> ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"8042" data-end=3D"8209" class=3D"">L'annotation <code data=
-start=3D"8055" data-end=3D"8067">@Component</code> est utilis=C3=A9e pour =
marquer une classe comme un bean Spring g=C3=A9n=C3=A9rique. Cela signifie =
que Spring va cr=C3=A9er et g=C3=A9rer une instance de cette classe.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"8211" data-end=3D"8294" class=3D"">5.2. Diff=C3=A9rences =
entre <code data-start=3D"8238" data-end=3D"8250">@Component</code>, <code =
data-start=3D"8252" data-end=3D"8262">@Service</code>, <code data-start=3D"=
8264" data-end=3D"8277">@Repository</code> et <code data-start=3D"8281" dat=
a-end=3D"8294">@Controller</code></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"8296" data-end=3D"8570">
<li data-start=3D"8296" data-end=3D"8366" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8298" data-end=3D"8366" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
298" data-end=3D"8312"><code data-start=3D"8300" data-end=3D"8310">@Service=
</code></strong> : Utilis=C3=A9e pour marquer une classe de service m=C3=A9=
tier.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8367" data-end=3D"8457" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8369" data-end=3D"8457" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
369" data-end=3D"8386"><code data-start=3D"8371" data-end=3D"8384">@Reposit=
ory</code></strong> : Utilis=C3=A9e pour marquer une classe de persistance =
(acc=C3=A8s aux donn=C3=A9es).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"8458" data-end=3D"8570" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"8460" data-end=3D"8570" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"8=
460" data-end=3D"8477"><code data-start=3D"8462" data-end=3D"8475">@Control=
ler</code></strong> : Utilis=C3=A9e dans les applications web pour marquer =
une classe comme un contr=C3=B4leur Spring MVC.</p>
</li>
</ul>
