<h3 data-start=3D"4347" data-end=3D"4393" class=3D"">2.1. Syntaxe de base p=
our d=C3=A9clarer un bean</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4395" data-end=3D"4567" class=3D"">Un bean est une simple =
instance d'une classe que Spring g=C3=A8re. La d=C3=A9claration d=E2=80=99u=
n bean en XML n=C3=A9cessite l'utilisation de la balise <code data-start=3D=
"4526" data-end=3D"4534">&lt;bean&gt;</code> avec deux attributs principaux=
 :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4569" data-end=3D"4642">
<li data-start=3D"4569" data-end=3D"4597" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4571" data-end=3D"4597" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
571" data-end=3D"4579"><code data-start=3D"4573" data-end=3D"4577">id</code=
></strong> : Le nom du bean.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4598" data-end=3D"4642" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4600" data-end=3D"4642" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
600" data-end=3D"4611"><code data-start=3D"4602" data-end=3D"4609">class</c=
ode></strong> : Le nom de la classe du bean.</p>
</li>
</ul>
