<h3 data-start=3D"9258" data-end=3D"9293" class=3D"">4.2. Annotations de ma=
ppage JPA</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"9295" data-end=3D"9507">
<li data-start=3D"9295" data-end=3D"9352" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"9297" data-end=3D"9352" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"9=
297" data-end=3D"9308">@Entity</strong> : Indique que la classe est une ent=
it=C3=A9 JPA.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9353" data-end=3D"9414" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"9355" data-end=3D"9414" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"9=
355" data-end=3D"9362">@Id</strong> : Sp=C3=A9cifie le champ qui repr=C3=A9=
sente la cl=C3=A9 primaire.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"9415" data-end=3D"9507" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"9417" data-end=3D"9507" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"9=
417" data-end=3D"9436">@GeneratedValue</strong> : D=C3=A9finit la strat=C3=
=A9gie de g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ration des valeurs pour la cl=C3=A9 primaire.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"9509" data-end=3D"9547" class=3D"">4.3. Gestion des ident=
ifiants (PK)</h3>
<p data-start=3D"9549" data-end=3D"9761" class=3D"">JPA n=C3=A9cessite une =
cl=C3=A9 primaire pour chaque entit=C3=A9. Par d=C3=A9faut, Hibernate g=C3=
=A8re automatiquement la g=C3=A9n=C3=A9ration des cl=C3=A9s primaires =C3=
=A0 l'aide de strat=C3=A9gies telles que <strong data-start=3D"9710" data-e=
nd=3D"9718">AUTO</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"9720" data-end=3D"9732">ID=
ENTITY</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"9734" data-end=3D"9746">SEQUENCE</st=
rong>, et <strong data-start=3D"9751" data-end=3D"9760">TABLE</strong>.</p>
