<ul data-start=3D"6157" data-end=3D"6432">
<li data-start=3D"6157" data-end=3D"6212" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6159" data-end=3D"6212" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
159" data-end=3D"6170">@Aspect</strong> : Indique que cette classe est un a=
spect.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6213" data-end=3D"6432" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6215" data-end=3D"6432" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
215" data-end=3D"6226">@Before</strong> : C'est un advice qui s'ex=C3=A9cut=
e avant le join point. L'expression <code data-start=3D"6293" data-end=3D"6=
334">execution(public * com.example.*.*(..))</code> d=C3=A9finit un pointcu=
t qui s'applique =C3=A0 toutes les m=C3=A9thodes publiques dans le package =
<code data-start=3D"6418" data-end=3D"6431">com.example</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6434" data-end=3D"6437" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6439" data-end=3D"6465" class=3D"">4. La Syntaxe d'Aspect=
J</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"6467" data-end=3D"6513" class=3D"">4.1. Les annotations p=
rincipales d'AspectJ</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6515" data-end=3D"6990">
<li data-start=3D"6515" data-end=3D"6571" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6517" data-end=3D"6571" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
517" data-end=3D"6528">@Aspect</strong> : Marque une classe comme =C3=A9tan=
t un aspect.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6572" data-end=3D"6638" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6574" data-end=3D"6638" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
574" data-end=3D"6585">@Before</strong> : D=C3=A9finit un conseil =C3=A0 ex=
=C3=A9cuter avant le join point.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6639" data-end=3D"6716" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6641" data-end=3D"6716" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
641" data-end=3D"6651">@After</strong> : D=C3=A9finit un conseil =C3=A0 ex=
=C3=A9cuter apr=C3=A8s l'ex=C3=A9cution du join point.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6717" data-end=3D"6810" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6719" data-end=3D"6810" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
719" data-end=3D"6730">@Around</strong> : Permet d'encadrer l'ex=C3=A9cutio=
n d'un join point, en modifiant son comportement.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6811" data-end=3D"6908" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6813" data-end=3D"6908" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
813" data-end=3D"6832">@AfterReturning</strong> : Ex=C3=A9cut=C3=A9 apr=C3=
=A8s que la m=C3=A9thode cible ait termin=C3=A9 son ex=C3=A9cution avec suc=
c=C3=A8s.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6909" data-end=3D"6990" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6911" data-end=3D"6990" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
911" data-end=3D"6929">@AfterThrowing</strong> : Ex=C3=A9cut=C3=A9 apr=C3=
=A8s que la m=C3=A9thode cible ait jet=C3=A9 une exception.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6992" data-end=3D"7028" class=3D"">4.2. Les expressions d=
e pointcut</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"7030" data-end=3D"7255">
<li data-start=3D"7030" data-end=3D"7087" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7032" data-end=3D"7087" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
032" data-end=3D"7050">execution(...)</strong> : Capture l'ex=C3=A9cution d=
'une m=C3=A9thode.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7088" data-end=3D"7182" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7090" data-end=3D"7182" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
090" data-end=3D"7105">within(...)</strong> : Capture l'ex=C3=A9cution de m=
=C3=A9thodes dans une classe ou un package particulier.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7183" data-end=3D"7255" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7185" data-end=3D"7255" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
185" data-end=3D"7198">args(...)</strong> : Capture les m=C3=A9thodes qui a=
cceptent certains arguments.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"7257" data-end=3D"7260" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"7262" data-end=3D"7296" class=3D"">5. Spring AOP : Un Cas=
 Pratique</h2>
<p data-start=3D"7298" data-end=3D"7524" class=3D"">Spring AOP (Aspect-Orie=
nted Programming) est une partie de Spring Framework qui permet d'utiliser =
la POA dans les applications Spring. Spring AOP repose sur le concept de <s=
trong data-start=3D"7469" data-end=3D"7479">proxys</strong> pour appliquer =
des aspects aux beans Spring.</p>
