<h3 data-start=3D"4701" data-end=3D"4719" class=3D"">Explications :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4720" data-end=3D"5008">
<li data-start=3D"4720" data-end=3D"4802" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4722" data-end=3D"4802" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
722" data-end=3D"4733">@Around</strong> : Nous encadrons l'ex=C3=A9cution d=
es m=C3=A9thodes annot=C3=A9es <code data-start=3D"4785" data-end=3D"4801">=
@Transactional</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4803" data-end=3D"4896" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4805" data-end=3D"4896" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
805" data-end=3D"4828">ProceedingJoinPoint</strong> : Il permet d'ex=C3=A9c=
uter la m=C3=A9thode cible et de g=C3=A9rer les exceptions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4897" data-end=3D"5008" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4899" data-end=3D"5008" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
899" data-end=3D"4922">Gestion des erreurs</strong> : Si une exception est =
lev=C3=A9e dans la m=C3=A9thode, la transaction sera annul=C3=A9e (rollback=
).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5010" data-end=3D"5117" class=3D"">Dans cet exemple, une t=
ransaction est g=C3=A9r=C3=A9e manuellement autour de chaque m=C3=A9thode a=
nnot=C3=A9e <code data-start=3D"5100" data-end=3D"5116">@Transactional</cod=
e>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"5119" data-end=3D"5122" class=3D"">
