t coh=C3=A9rent.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4004" data-end=3D"4041" class=3D"">Quand utiliser <code d=
ata-start=3D"4023" data-end=3D"4039">@Transactional</code> ?</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4043" data-end=3D"4243">
<li data-start=3D"4043" data-end=3D"4150" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4045" data-end=3D"4150" class=3D"">Sur des <strong data-st=
art=3D"4053" data-end=3D"4076">m=C3=A9thodes de service</strong> o=C3=B9 pl=
usieurs op=C3=A9rations doivent =C3=AAtre ex=C3=A9cut=C3=A9es dans une m=C3=
=AAme transaction.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4151" data-end=3D"4243" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4153" data-end=3D"4243" class=3D"">Sur des <strong data-st=
art=3D"4161" data-end=3D"4187">m=C3=A9thodes de repository</strong> pour ga=
rantir la coh=C3=A9rence des actions sur les donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4245" data-end=3D"4248" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4250" data-end=3D"4302" class=3D"">3. Fonctionnement de <=
code data-start=3D"4274" data-end=3D"4290">@Transactional</code> dans Sprin=
g</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4304" data-end=3D"4332" class=3D"">Gestion des Transactio=
ns</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4334" data-end=3D"4596" class=3D"">Spring g=C3=A8re la tra=
nsaction pour nous gr=C3=A2ce au m=C3=A9canisme <strong data-start=3D"4390"=
 data-end=3D"4397">AOP</strong> (Aspect-Oriented Programming). Lorsque vous=
 appliquez l=E2=80=99annotation <code data-start=3D"4465" data-end=3D"4481"=
>@Transactional</code> sur une m=C3=A9thode, Spring cr=C3=A9e un <strong da=
ta-start=3D"4514" data-end=3D"4523">proxy</strong> autour de cette m=C3=A9t=
hode pour g=C3=A9rer le d=C3=A9but et la fin de la transaction.</p>
<ol data-start=3D"4598" data-end=3D"4909">
<li data-start=3D"4598" data-end=3D"4656" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4601" data-end=3D"4656" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
601" data-end=3D"4622">Avant l'ex=C3=A9cution</strong> : Spring d=C3=A9marr=
e une transaction.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4657" data-end=3D"4739" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4660" data-end=3D"4739" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
660" data-end=3D"4687">Ex=C3=A9cution de la m=C3=A9thode</strong> : La m=C3=
=A9thode de service ou repository est ex=C3=A9cut=C3=A9e.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4740" data-end=3D"4909" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4743" data-end=3D"4909" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
743" data-end=3D"4764">Apr=C3=A8s l'ex=C3=A9cution</strong> : Si la m=C3=A9=
thode se termine sans erreur, la transaction est valid=C3=A9e (commit). Si =
une exception est lanc=C3=A9e, la transaction est annul=C3=A9e (rollback).<=
/p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"4911" data-end=3D"4929" class=3D"">Types de Proxy</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4931" data-end=3D"5034" class=3D"">Spring cr=C3=A9e des pr=
oxies autour des beans annot=C3=A9s avec <code data-start=3D"4985" data-end=
=3D"5001">@Transactional</code>. Il existe deux types de proxy :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5036" data-end=3D"5290">
<li data-start=3D"5036" data-end=3D"5172" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5038" data-end=3D"5172" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
038" data-end=3D"5051">Proxy JDK</strong> (par d=C3=A9faut) : Cr=C3=A9e un =
proxy bas=C3=A9 sur l'interface du bean. Ce proxy fonctionne si votre class=
e impl=C3=A9mente une interface.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5173" data-end=3D"5290" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5175" data-end=3D"5290" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
175" data-end=3D"5190">Proxy CGLIB</strong> : Cr=C3=A9e un proxy bas=C3=A9 =
sur la classe. Ce proxy est utilis=C3=A9 si la classe n'impl=C3=A9mente pas=
 d'interface.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"5292" data-end=3D"5295" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"5297" data-end=3D"5374" class=3D"">4. Personnalisation du=
 Comportement des Transactions avec <code data-start=3D"5358" data-end=3D"5=
374">@Transactional</code></h2>
<p data-start=3D"5376" data-end=3D"5546" class=3D"">L'annotation <code data=
-start=3D"5389" data-end=3D"5405">@Transactional</code> offre plusieurs att=
ributs qui vous permettent de personnaliser son comportement. Voici les pri=
ncipaux attributs que vous pouvez configurer :</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"5548" data-end=3D"5581" class=3D"">Attributs de <code dat=
a-start=3D"5565" data-end=3D"5581">@Transactional</code></h3>
<h4 data-start=3D"5583" data-end=3D"5606" class=3D"">1. <strong data-start=
=3D"5591" data-end=3D"5606">propagation</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"5608" data-end=3D"5774" class=3D"">Le type de <strong data=
-start=3D"5619" data-end=3D"5634">propagation</strong> d=C3=A9finit la mani=
=C3=A8re dont les transactions sont g=C3=A9r=C3=A9es lorsqu'une m=C3=A9thod=
e est appel=C3=A9e depuis une autre m=C3=A9thode annot=C3=A9e avec <code da=
ta-start=3D"5757" data-end=3D"5773">@Transactional</code>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"5776" data-end=3D"5828" class=3D"">Les options de propagat=
ion les plus courantes sont :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5830" data-end=3D"6138">
<li data-start=3D"5830" data-end=3D"5953" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5832" data-end=3D"5953" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
832" data-end=3D"5844">REQUIRED</strong> (par d=C3=A9faut) : Si une transac=
tion existe d=C3=A9j=C3=A0, elle est utilis=C3=A9e. Sinon, une nouvelle tra=
nsaction est cr=C3=A9=C3=A9e.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5954" data-end=3D"6059" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5956" data-end=3D"6059" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
956" data-end=3D"5972">REQUIRES_NEW</strong> : Une nouvelle transaction est=
 toujours d=C3=A9marr=C3=A9e, suspendant la transaction existante.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6060" data-end=3D"6138" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6062" data-end=3D"6138" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
062" data-end=3D"6072">NESTED</strong> : Si une transaction existe, une tra=
nsaction imbriqu=C3=A9e est cr=C3=A9=C3=A9e.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"6140" data-end=3D"6149" class=3D"">Exemple :</p>
