<h2 data-start=3D"4174" data-end=3D"4212" class=3D"">3. Concepts de base de=
 Spring Batch</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"4214" data-end=3D"4266" class=3D"">Job, Step, ItemReader,=
 ItemProcessor, ItemWriter</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4268" data-end=3D"4325" class=3D"">Spring Batch repose sur=
 plusieurs concepts fondamentaux :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4326" data-end=3D"4776">
<li data-start=3D"4326" data-end=3D"4421" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4328" data-end=3D"4421" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
328" data-end=3D"4335">Job</strong> : Un job repr=C3=A9sente l'ensemble du =
processus batch. Il peut contenir plusieurs =C3=A9tapes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4422" data-end=3D"4489" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4424" data-end=3D"4489" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
424" data-end=3D"4432">Step</strong> : Une =C3=A9tape repr=C3=A9sente une u=
nit=C3=A9 de travail dans un job.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4490" data-end=3D"4586" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4492" data-end=3D"4586" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
492" data-end=3D"4506">ItemReader</strong> : L'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ment qui lit le=
s donn=C3=A9es (depuis une base de donn=C3=A9es, un fichier, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4587" data-end=3D"4661" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4589" data-end=3D"4661" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
589" data-end=3D"4606">ItemProcessor</strong> : L'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ment qui tra=
ite et transforme les donn=C3=A9es lues.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4662" data-end=3D"4776" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4664" data-end=3D"4776" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
664" data-end=3D"4678">ItemWriter</strong> : L'=C3=A9l=C3=A9ment qui =C3=A9=
crit les donn=C3=A9es trait=C3=A9es dans une destination (base de donn=C3=
=A9es, fichier, etc.).</p>
</li>
</ul>
